{"id":"leetcode-321","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Create Maximum Number","summary":"Given two integer arrays representing digits of two numbers and an integer k, create the maximum number of length k from the digits while preserving the relative order within each array.","statement":"Given two integer arrays representing digits of two numbers and an integer k, create the maximum number of length k from the digits while preserving the relative order within each array. Return an array of k digits.","constraints":["nums1 and nums2 each contain 1–500 digits from 0 through 9, without leading zeros; 1 <= k <= len(nums1)+len(nums2).","Choose exactly k digits in total. You may interleave the arrays freely, but must preserve the order of the chosen digits from EACH array. Return the lexicographically largest length-k digit list."],"topics":["greedy","stacks","strings","arrays"],"prerequisites":["arrays","stacks"],"signature":{"name":"create_maximum_number","parameters":[{"name":"nums1","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"nums2","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"k","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[int]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def create_maximum_number(nums1: list[int], nums2: list[int], k: int) -> list[int]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def create_maximum_number(nums1, nums2, k):\n    def select(values, count):\n        drop = len(values)-count\n        stack = []\n        for value in values:\n            while drop and stack and stack[-1] < value:\n                stack.pop()\n                drop -= 1\n            stack.append(value)\n        return ''.join(str(value) for value in stack[:count])\n    best = ''\n    for count in range(max(0,k-len(nums2)), min(k,len(nums1))+1):\n        left, right = select(nums1,count), select(nums2,k-count)\n        merged = []\n        while left or right:\n            if left > right:\n                merged.append(left[0])\n                left = left[1:]\n            else:\n                merged.append(right[0])\n                right = right[1:]\n        best = max(best, ''.join(merged))\n    return [int(digit) for digit in best]\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def create_maximum_number(nums1, nums2, k):\n    return sorted(nums1+nums2, reverse=True)[:k]\n","def create_maximum_number(nums1, nums2, k):\n    def select(values, count):\n        drop = len(values)-count\n        stack = []\n        for value in values:\n            while drop and stack and stack[-1] < value:\n                stack.pop()\n                drop -= 1\n            stack.append(value)\n        return ''.join(str(value) for value in stack[:count])\n    best = ''\n    for count in range(max(0,k-len(nums2)), min(k,len(nums1))+1):\n        left, right = select(nums1,count), select(nums2,k-count)\n        merged = []\n        while left or right:\n            if left[:1] >= right[:1]:\n                merged.append(left[0])\n                left = left[1:]\n            else:\n                merged.append(right[0])\n                right = right[1:]\n        best = max(best, ''.join(merged))\n    return [int(digit) for digit in best]\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(s*(m+n+k^2)), s = feasible split count","target_space_complexity":"O(m+n+k)","estimated_minutes":50,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":3,"prerequisites":2,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":1},"hints":["Try each feasible split of the k selected digits between the two arrays.","For a fixed split, use a monotone stack to choose the largest subsequence of the required length from each array.","Merge those subsequences by comparing their entire remaining suffixes, not just their first digits; keep the best merge across splits.","A removal budget controls each stack. Equal heads require looking ahead; if one suffix is a prefix of the other, the longer suffix is larger."],"editorial":"Every answer has some allocation of selected positions to the two inputs. For each allocation, greedily deleting a smaller earlier digit when enough positions remain yields each largest fixed-length subsequence. The maximal interleaving always consumes from the lexicographically larger remaining suffix; comparing only the first digit fails on ties. Enumerate feasible allocations and keep the greatest resulting list. The oracle directly enumerates every legal next index in either array with memoization, independently of split selection and greedy merging.","tests":[{"id":"lc-321-1","arguments":[[3,4,6,5],[9,1,2,5,8,3],5],"expected":[9,8,6,5,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Choose [6,5] from nums1 and [9,8,3] from nums2, then interleave them as [9,8,6,5,3]. Both within-array orders are preserved.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-2","arguments":[[6,0,4],[6,7],5],"expected":[6,7,6,0,4],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Both next digits are 6, but the suffix [6,7] is larger than [6,0,4]. Take it first to obtain [6,7,6,0,4].","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-3","arguments":[[1],[2],1],"expected":[2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-4","arguments":[[1],[2],2],"expected":[2,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-5","arguments":[[0],[0],1],"expected":[0],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-6","arguments":[[9],[1,2],2],"expected":[9,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-7","arguments":[[3,9],[8,9],3],"expected":[9,8,9],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-8","arguments":[[6,7],[6,0,4],5],"expected":[6,7,6,0,4],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-9","arguments":[[8,1,9],[8,2],4],"expected":[8,9,8,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-10","arguments":[[9,0,1],[8,9],3],"expected":[9,9,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-11","arguments":[[1,2,3],[4,5,6],3],"expected":[6,2,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-12","arguments":[[9,8],[7,6],4],"expected":[9,8,7,6],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-13","arguments":[[1,1],[1,1],3],"expected":[1,1,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-14","arguments":[[9,1],[9,0],3],"expected":[9,9,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-15","arguments":[[2,5,6,4],[4,3,8],5],"expected":[8,2,5,6,4],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-16","arguments":[[7,0,0],[7,0,1],6],"expected":[7,7,0,1,0,0],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-321-stress-1","arguments":[[9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,9,